<</Type/StructElem/S/H4/P 375 0 R/T(Plenary - Bridging Cultural Divides: Interactive Strategies for Culturally Responsive ELICOS Teaching - Presented by Marcela Lapertosa from Value Learning \(10.00-11.00\))/E(Plenary - Bridging Cultural Divides: Interactive Strategies for Culturally Responsive ELICOS Teaching - Presented by Marcela Lapertosa from Value Learning \(10.00-11.00\))/Pg 13 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

139 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 376 0 R/E(UQ Voices will be performing 3 crowd-pleasers, guaranteed to entertain and delight the Qld PD Fest crowd!)/Pg 13 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

140 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 376 0 R/E(Know someone who might enjoy or benefit from the choir? Connect with UQ Voices on Instagram: @uq_voices)/Pg 13 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

141 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 377 0 R/E(Join English Australia\220s CEO, Ian Aird, for a brief video update covering the latest legislation and policy changes shaping the ELICOS sector. Ian will break down what these developments mean for you and your students \204 clearly, concisely, and with in a way that\220s relevant to you.)/Pg 13 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

142 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 378 0 R/E(As ELICOS programs welcome increasingly diverse international cohorts, educators must understand how different cultural and educational backgrounds shape learning preferences and classroom expectations. This interactive workshop led Marcela Lapertosa, a cross-cultural psychologist, examines cultural variations in teaching and learning styles and the importance of adapting pedagogical approaches for multicultural classrooms. Drawing on research and practical examples, participants will actively explore how cultural values, previous educational experiences, and communication norms influence students' engagement, participation, and learning. Through small group activities and case study discussions, attendees will identify challenges faced by learners from collectivist versus individualist cultures, high-context versus low-context communication backgrounds, and varied educational traditions.)/Pg 13 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

143 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 378 0 R/E(The workshop provides evidence-based strategies for creating inclusive learning environments, including adapting questioning techniques, and recognising how unconscious assumptions about classroom participation can impact student success. Participants will leave with practical tools for fostering cross-cultural awareness, building rapport across cultural boundaries, and creating flexible learning pathways that honour diverse approaches to language learning while maintaining academic rigour in ELICOS contexts.)/Pg 13 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

144 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H5/P 379 0 R/T(UQ Voices is a Brisbane-based community choir for international students and friends, dedicated to promoting wellbeing and belonging on campus and in the wider community. Founded by the UQ School of Psychology and proudly supported by The Queensland Institute since 2021, UQ Voices brings people together through the joy of group singing and contributes to research outcomes in international student wellbeing. )/E(UQ Voices is a Brisbane-based community choir for international students and friends, dedicated to promoting wellbeing and belonging on campus and in the wider community. Founded by the UQ School of Psychology and proudly supported by The Queensland Institute since 2021, UQ Voices brings people together through the joy of group singing and contributes to research outcomes in international student wellbeing. )/Pg 13 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

145 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H5/P 380 0 R/T(Ian has over 25 years\220 experience in international education, spanning the full ELICOS sector. He began as a teacher and CELTA trainer, progressed to Director of Studies, and later led across sales and marketing, admissions, IT, and executive management. He also ran a consulting firm for five years, advising on strategy, M&A, financial performance, market and economic research, regulatory reform and compliance, and executive and sales coaching, with clients including government agencies, industry bodies, and education providers from universities to multinational and family-owned organisations. His governance experience includes six years on the English Australia Board, serving on the StudyNSW advisory board, and five years as non-executive Chair of a not-for-profit. He holds a Graduate Diploma in Law, an MBA with Distinction, a Masters in Professional Education, and completed the AICD Company Directors Course with Order of Merit, along with CELTA and DELTA qualifications.)/E(Ian has over 25 years\220 experience in international education, spanning the full ELICOS sector. He began as a teacher and CELTA trainer, progressed to Director of Studies, and later led across sales and marketing, admissions, IT, and executive management. He also ran a consulting firm for five years, advising on strategy, M&A, financial performance, market and economic research, regulatory reform and compliance, and executive and sales coaching, with clients including government agencies, industry bodies, and education providers from universities to multinational and family-owned organisations. His governance experience includes six years on the English Australia Board, serving on the StudyNSW advisory board, and five years as non-executive Chair of a not-for-profit. He holds a Graduate Diploma in Law, an MBA with Distinction, a Masters in Professional Education, and completed the AICD Company Directors Course with Order of Merit, along with CELTA and DELTA qualifications.)/Pg 13 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

146 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H5/P 381 0 R/T(A cross-cultural psychologist with a passion for fostering intercultural understanding, Marcela is a master facilitator and trainer who has travelled the world leading the development and delivery of global competence curricula, intercultural learning, and leadership training to diverse audiences. As co-founder of Value Learning, a Corporate Affiliate of English Australia and a consulting business committed to advancing global competence and fostering intercultural understanding, Marcela brings extensive expertise in bridging cultural divides and creating inclusive learning environments across educational contexts.)/E(A cross-cultural psychologist with a passion for fostering intercultural understanding, Marcela is a master facilitator and trainer who has travelled the world leading the development and delivery of global competence curricula, intercultural learning, and leadership training to diverse audiences. As co-founder of Value Learning, a Corporate Affiliate of English Australia and a consulting business committed to advancing global competence and fostering intercultural understanding, Marcela brings extensive expertise in bridging cultural divides and creating inclusive learning environments across educational contexts.)/Pg 13 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

