186 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H4/P 402 0 R/T(Meaningful goal setting for ESL learnings \205 Turning aspirations into action! - Presented by Jennifer Allan \(11.30-12.00\))/E(Meaningful goal setting for ESL learnings \205 Turning aspirations into action! - Presented by Jennifer Allan \(11.30-12.00\))/Pg 16 0 R/K[0]>>
endobj

187 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H4/P 403 0 R/T(Mentimeter: Interactive learning to spark student engagement - Presented by Timothy Green  \(12.05-12.35\))/E(Mentimeter: Interactive learning to spark student engagement - Presented by Timothy Green  \(12.05-12.35\))/Pg 16 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

188 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H4/P 404 0 R/T(The best of both worlds: Developing reading skills with authentic texts and a little AI help - Presented by Sophie Walker \(12.05-12.35\))/E(The best of both worlds: Developing reading skills with authentic texts and a little AI help - Presented by Sophie Walker \(12.05-12.35\))/Pg 16 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

189 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 405 0 R/E(Supporting English language learners to create goals that are clear, purposeful, motivating and tailored to their learning needs helps them to take ownership of their progress. In this session I\220d like to share some classroom-ready strategies for guiding students to create tangible language learning goals that build confidence and long-term growth. )/Pg 16 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

190 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 405 0 R/E(Having achievable but challenging goals in place provides structure and as a result can improve study habits, facilitate stronger progress tracking and creates better alignment between classroom tasks and learner aims. )/Pg 16 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

191 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 405 0 R/E(Attendees will explore what makes a goal \215meaningful\220 in an ESL context, leaving the session with tools to guide students to set their own short and longer-term goals. In addition, the session will cover ways of embedding reflection and self-monitoring into everyday classroom and self-study learning. )/Pg 16 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

192 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 405 0 R/E(Ideal for teachers looking to strengthen student engagement and create a greater sense of achievement for short and long-term students alike by propelling them out of \217stagnation\220 in their learning journeys! )/Pg 16 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

193 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 406 0 R/E(Ready to move beyond basic quiz tools to provide an easy to use yet effective interactive online tool? While platforms like Kahoot, Canva, and Genially have their place, Mentimeter offers a surprisingly powerful number of features that can transform how students interact, collaborate, and learn together.)/Pg 16 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

194 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 406 0 R/E(My presentation is hands-on and showcases Mentimeter's versatility through live demonstrations that teachers can immediately apply in their own context. We'll explore three applications of Mentimeter: quizzes, designing task-based collaborative activities, and facilitating open-ended whole class discussion-based activities that spark genuine engagement.)/Pg 16 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

195 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 406 0 R/E(This will involve moving beyond the basics of Mentimeter as a polling tool and exploring features such as scales and rankings, different visual representations for multiple choice questions, AI summaries of creative Q&A sessions, and collaborative brainstorming that work across all proficiency levels from general English to EAP and more. My presentation will also touch on AI tools that can create for Mentimeter, such as Menti AI assistant and Claude Anthropic.)/Pg 16 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

196 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 406 0 R/E(While each competing platform has its specific areas of strength, this presentation covers exactly when and where Mentimeter can outperform the alternatives. Leave this session with practical, ready-to use strategies and the confidence to implement Mentimeter effectively from day one.)/Pg 16 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

197 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 407 0 R/E(This presentation will focus on one short authentic text to argue that if we want to develop our students\220 reading skills and maintain our assessment writing skills, we should be using human-generated texts in our classrooms and tests. We will look at how AI can play a role in helping us prepare reading material for the classroom and assessments \205 but not as the \217author\220 of the text we want to use with students.)/Pg 16 0 R/K[11]>>
endobj

198 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H5/P 408 0 R/T(A multi-lingual ESL trainer with 10 years industry experience having worked as an English Assistant in Paris before embarking on a career in the cooperate and VET RTO world during which time I ran PD workshops and training for employees focusing on professional growth and career advancement. Moving into the ESL industry in Brisbane ignited my passion for supporting international students in the classroom, specifically looking at ways to catapult their progress and build their self-confidence!)/E(A multi-lingual ESL trainer with 10 years industry experience having worked as an English Assistant in Paris before embarking on a career in the cooperate and VET RTO world during which time I ran PD workshops and training for employees focusing on professional growth and career advancement. Moving into the ESL industry in Brisbane ignited my passion for supporting international students in the classroom, specifically looking at ways to catapult their progress and build their self-confidence!)/Pg 16 0 R/K[12]>>
endobj

199 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H5/P 409 0 R/T(I am a passionate ESL/ELT educator with over 15 years of experience. Much of my career was spent at a local English school that ranked as high as 3rd globally and for the past two years, I've been working with a dedicated team at Bond University. My primary focus is teaching the interrelationship between vocabulary and grammar, while exploring technology-assisted learning to create effective and engaging classroom experiences. I look forward to sharing insights and connecting with colleagues at this professional development festival.)/E(I am a passionate ESL/ELT educator with over 15 years of experience. Much of my career was spent at a local English school that ranked as high as 3rd globally and for the past two years, I've been working with a dedicated team at Bond University. My primary focus is teaching the interrelationship between vocabulary and grammar, while exploring technology-assisted learning to create effective and engaging classroom experiences. I look forward to sharing insights and connecting with colleagues at this professional development festival.)/Pg 16 0 R/K[13]>>
endobj

200 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H5/P 410 0 R/T(I work at UQ College as part of the assessment team producing tests for the English language pathways programs and tests for use in the wider university. I have a passion for item writing and continuing to develop my own skills as well as the skills of other item writers and teachers, especially in the age of AI where these skills are in danger of being eroded. )/E(I work at UQ College as part of the assessment team producing tests for the English language pathways programs and tests for use in the wider university. I have a passion for item writing and continuing to develop my own skills as well as the skills of other item writers and teachers, especially in the age of AI where these skills are in danger of being eroded. )/Pg 16 0 R/K[14]>>
