endobj

243 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 429 0 R/E(The new science of stress: Turning pressure into academic performance - Presented by Faye Lawand \(1.30-2.00\))/Pg 19 0 R/K[0]>>
endobj

244 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 430 0 R/E(Closing Plenary - Beyond burnout: Cultivating wellbeing for ELICOS professionals - Presented by Dr Patrick Pheasant \(2.10-3.00\))/Pg 19 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

245 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 431 0 R/E(ELICOS classes focused on high-stakes exams come with high expectations, diverse language proficiency levels, and relentless performance demands. But what if stress isn\220t just an obstacle, but a lever for learning?)/Pg 19 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

246 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 431 0 R/E(This session brings forward groundbreaking research from Stanford University on the New Science of Stress, busting the old myths and revealing how acute pressure \(when reframed\) can enhance focus, memory, and motivation in both students and teachers. We\220ll unpack the latest neuroscience and psychophysiology, showing how stress, managed differently, can move from sabotage to support.)/Pg 19 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

247 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 431 0 R/E(You\220ll walk through the key findings, see what this means in your own classroom, and experience a practical reframing process. No jargon, no complicated tools, just a new lens you can use immediately to benefit yourself and your learners.)/Pg 19 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

248 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 432 0 R/E(In the demanding ELICOS sector, teacher well-being is the foundation of student success and institutional resilience. Yet, navigating complex classroom dynamics, regulatory pressures, and student pastoral care often leads to chronic stress and compassion fatigue.)/Pg 19 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

249 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 432 0 R/E(Drawing on clinical psychotherapy and international education leadership, this session explores the hidden drivers of teacher burnout through real-world case studies. Moving from diagnosis to actionable intervention, we will examine a multi-layered approach to building psychological safety:)/Pg 19 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

250 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 432 0 R/E(\200 The School: Systemic strategies for leadership to structurally support staff mental health.)/Pg 19 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

251 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 432 0 R/E(\200 The Colleagues: Practical ways to build supportive, peer-led staffroom cultures.)/Pg 19 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

252 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 432 0 R/E(\200 The Individual: Evidence-based tools to regulate stress and build embodied resilience.)/Pg 19 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

253 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 432 0 R/E(Attendees will be encouraged to consider a "Well-being Action Plan" to advocate for healthier workplace dynamics, support their peers, and sustainably protect their own energy and passion for teaching.)/Pg 19 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

254 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 433 0 R/E(Faye Lawand is a seasoned educator with over 20 years of experience in teaching and teacher training across a wide range of educational settings from elementary to university, in diverse international contexts. She holds a Master of Arts in Education \(ESOL\) and is a certified clinical hypnotherapist, Advanced Relaxation Teacher, and Master Practitioner of NLP. Along the way, Faye noticed a crucial piece missing from traditional teacher training: practical tools for self-regulation and personal agency. Today, she integrates brain-based learning with nervous system support to fill that gap, equipping students and educators with science-backed strategies to reduce stress, sharpen focus, and build the resilience needed to thrive in high-pressure environments.)/Pg 19 0 R/K[11]>>
endobj

255 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 434 0 R/E(Dr Patrick Pheasant is the Head of Education Partnerships \(ANZ\) at LanguageCert and a registered psychotherapist and counsellor. With over 30 years of experience in international education, including seven years as CEO of NEAS Australia, Patrick intimately understands the unique systemic and classroom pressures placed on ELICOS professionals. Holding a PhD in Education with a focus on embodied learning, he merges his extensive sector leadership with clinical mental health expertise. Patrick is a passionate advocate for creating psychologically safe, resilient environments where both educators and students can thrive.)/Pg 19 0 R/K[12]>>
endobj

