713 0 obj
<</Title(The best of both worlds: Developing reading skills with authentic texts and a little AI help - Presented by Sophie Walker \(12.05-12.35\))/Dest[16 0 R/Fit]/Parent 539 0 R/Prev 712 0 R/First 758 0 R/Last 759 0 R/Count -3/Next 659 0 R>>
endobj

714 0 obj
<</Title(As generative AI reshapes student writing and learning, pathways programs face growing pressure to uphold academic integrity while preparing students for university expectations. This session argues that key intellectual and academic skills that are vital for students\220 ability to engage ethically with AI are often assumed rather than explicitly taught in pathways curricula. Drawing on higher education practice and current research in progress, the presentation suggests opportunities for pathway programs to take a steering role in preparing students for first-year university demands in relation to engagement with AI. It will argue that doing so requires educators to harness the critical thinking capabilities already present in the cohort, as well as provide students with the practical skills required to assess the validity of source material and demonstrate effective argumentation. Participants will explore practical strategies for embedding critical thinking through scaffolded tasks, metacognitive reflection, and assessment design that prioritises process over product.)/Dest[17 0 R/Fit]/Parent 661 0 R/Next 760 0 R>>
endobj

715 0 obj
<</Title(She enjoys creating engaging materials including students\220 books, workbooks and supplementary resources for learners worldwide. She is currently passionate about Teacher\220s Guides as a powerful yet often underused tool for supporting teachers and enriching lessons.)/Dest[17 0 R/Fit]/Parent 661 0 R/Prev 761 0 R>>
endobj

716 0 obj
<</Title(Sermin Erden is an experienced language educator with a strong interest in the relationship between language, cognition, and communication in multilingual contexts. Her previous work explored how linguistic differences are often mistaken for cultural differences in second language learning and teaching. Building on this, her current focus brings language and culture together through the lens of grammar, examining how meaning, nuance, and social expectations are encoded and taught in English. She is passionate about helping teachers better understand multilingual learners and classroom communication.)/Dest[18 0 R/Fit]/Parent 543 0 R/Prev 662 0 R/Next 717 0 R>>
endobj

717 0 obj
<</Title(Jo Kwai is a QCT registered, experienced teacher and has worked in the schools sector \(public and private\), ELICOS, TAFE AMEP, VET Trainer and Assessor \(TESOL\); Jo has also been an Academic Manager, and is currently on the secondary school team at St Peters Lutheran College, as a CLA-EALD, and International Student Coordinator.  She is also a current board member of the federal govt Tuition Protection Service \(TPS\).)/Dest[18 0 R/Fit]/Parent 543 0 R/Prev 716 0 R/Next 663 0 R>>
endobj

