<</Title(Cambridge capers: Serious learning, playful practice - Presented by Bec Hungerford \(11.30-12.30\))/Dest[14 0 R/Fit]/Parent 709 0 R/Prev 754 0 R/Next 768 0 R>>
endobj

768 0 obj
<</Title(Write more, work less \(Without AI\) - Presented by Neridah McHenry \(11.30-12.30\))/Dest[14 0 R/Fit]/Parent 709 0 R/Prev 767 0 R/First 778 0 R/Last 779 0 R/Count -3/Next 755 0 R>>
endobj

769 0 obj
<</Title(Chiaki has over 25 years of experience catering to students from diverse backgrounds and ages. She has taught at various private and government institutions in Australia and Japan. She specialises in pre and in-service teacher training. Her focus as an educator is World Englishes, cross-cultural identity, and communication. At SCU College, she is a teaching scholar, and her primary role is to oversee the English Language Program and provide student support across campuses.)/Dest[15 0 R/Fit]/Parent 757 0 R/Next 780 0 R>>
endobj

770 0 obj
<</Title(An experienced educator and teacher educator specialising in EAP, TESOL, and Applied Linguistics, with a strong focus on writing pedagogy and feedback. He has extensive experience in curriculum design, pedagogical innovation, and academic language development in tertiary contexts. His work emphasises culturally responsive teaching, plurilingualism, and theory-informed use of Generative AI in language education. He has led teams, developed institutional resources, and taught across face-to-face, blended, and online programs. His current interests include feedback literacy, teacher development, and technology-enhanced learning.)/Dest[15 0 R/Fit]/Parent 757 0 R/Prev 781 0 R>>
endobj

771 0 obj
<</Title(I am a passionate ESL/ELT educator with over 15 years of experience. Much of my career was spent at a local English school that ranked as high as 3rd globally and for the past two years, I've been working with a dedicated team at Bond University. My primary focus is teaching the interrelationship between vocabulary and grammar, while exploring technology-assisted learning to create effective and engaging classroom experiences. I look forward to sharing insights and connecting with colleagues at this professional development festival.)/Dest[16 0 R/Fit]/Parent 713 0 R/Prev 758 0 R/Next 759 0 R>>
endobj

772 0 obj
<</Title(Teacher\220s Guides are written for teachers, yet they are frequently underused or overlooked. At best, they might be consulted to check answer keys, at worst, teachers may not even receive a copy.  However, most Teacher\220s Guides are packed with resources which, when used or adapted, can save valuable preparation time, enrich lessons and even serve as a form of ongoing professional development. This is a practical workshop, and participants will engage in hands-on activities including trying out the writing of their own teacher\220s notes for an activity and also discovering some hidden gems within the Guides. There will also be plenty of opportunities to share experiences and ideas.  Participants will leave with a toolkit of creative, ready-to-use ideas that will encourage closer reading of Teacher\220s Guides, enhanced coursebook use and inspiration for classroom practice.)/Dest[17 0 R/Fit]/Parent 661 0 R/Prev 760 0 R/Next 782 0 R>>
endobj

773 0 obj
<</Title(Cole is a passionate educator with experience across a range of educational contexts.  As a seasoned EAL instructor, he is enthusiastic about working towards a future of helping the next generation of teachers get started and build confidence in this exciting industry.)/Dest[17 0 R/Fit]/Parent 661 0 R/Prev 782 0 R/Next 761 0 R>>
endobj

774 0 obj
<</Title(9.45 - 10.00)/Dest[9 0 R/Fit]/Parent 268 0 R/Prev 763 0 R/Next 783 0 R>>
endobj

775 0 obj
<</Title(The New Science of Stress: Turning Pressure into Academic Performance Faye Lawand)/Dest[9 0 R/Fit]/Parent 268 0 R/Prev 784 0 R/Next 764 0 R>>
endobj

776 0 obj
<</Title(UQ Voices is a Brisbane-based community choir for international students and friends, dedicated to promoting wellbeing and belonging on campus and in the wider community. Founded by the UQ School of Psychology and proudly supported by The Queensland Institute since 2021, UQ Voices brings people together through the joy of group singing and contributes to research outcomes in international student wellbeing.)/Dest[13 0 R/Fit]/Parent 766 0 R/Next 785 0 R>>
endobj

777 0 obj
<</Title(A cross-cultural psychologist with a passion for fostering intercultural understanding, Marcela is a master facilitator and trainer who has travelled the world leading the development and delivery of global competence curricula, intercultural learning, and leadership training to diverse audiences. As co-founder of Value Learning, a Corporate Affiliate of English Australia and a consulting business committed to advancing global competence and fostering intercultural understanding, Marcela brings extensive expertise in bridging cultural divides and creating inclusive learning environments across educational contexts.)/Dest[13 0 R/Fit]/Parent 766 0 R/Prev 785 0 R>>
endobj

778 0 obj
<</Title(Nathaniel Mitchell is formally trained in Phonetics at Griffith University, lecturing into phonetics and phonology from 2013 until 2018. His Honors project specifically looked at pronunciation of Australian English and worked on the Western Australian English Pronunciation project with Griffith University.)/Dest[14 0 R/Fit]/Parent 768 0 R/Next 786 0 R>>
endobj

779 0 obj
<</Title(Neridah got her CELTA some 14 years ago with the intention of working overseas long enough to sound interesting at parties. She has gone on to love of the challenge of EAP and IELTs courses and completed a Masters of Teaching in 2021. Her great loves are books, trivia, and teachable moments.)/Dest[14 0 R/Fit]/Parent 768 0 R/Prev 786 0 R>>
endobj

780 0 obj
<</Title(John Day is an English language teacher at UQ College with over ten years\220 experience in TESOL teaching, teacher training, and academic leadership in Australia and China. Alongside his ongoing classroom teaching, he contributes to curriculum design, quality assurance, and professional development, and has delivered workshops on pedagogy and educational technology. He is particularly interested in exploring how AI can be integrated into TESOL in ways that strengthen learner thinking, confidence, and meaningful communication.)/Dest[15 0 R/Fit]/Parent 757 0 R/Prev 769 0 R/Next 781 0 R>>
endobj

781 0 obj
<</Title(Katie Clancy has worked across Australian mainstream schools and English programs in South America, and has spent the past 10 years at UQ College. Her work spans university preparation programs and Learning Advice, supporting diverse learners in academic contexts. Grounded in cross-cultural experience, Katie is committed to equity, student voice, and reflective practice. She values curiosity, collaboration, and ongoing professional growth, and is interested in how educational technology and AI can support confidence, critical thinking, and independent academic identities.)/Dest[15 0 R/Fit]/Parent 757 0 R/Prev 780 0 R/Next 770 0 R>>
endobj

