784 0 obj
<</Title(Navigating the Whys and the hows of being an early career ELICOS teacher Jo Kwai & Donna Cook)/Dest[9 0 R/Fit]/Parent 268 0 R/Prev 788 0 R/Next 775 0 R>>
endobj

785 0 obj
<</Title(Ian has over 25 years\220 experience in international education, spanning the full ELICOS sector. He began as a teacher and CELTA trainer, progressed to Director of Studies, and later led across sales and marketing, admissions, IT, and executive management. He also ran a consulting firm for five years, advising on strategy, M&A, financial performance, market and economic research, regulatory reform and compliance, and executive and sales coaching, with clients including government agencies, industry bodies, and education providers from universities to multinational and family-owned organisations. His governance experience includes six years on the English Australia Board, serving on the StudyNSW advisory board, and five years as non-executive Chair of a not-for-profit. He holds a Graduate Diploma in Law, an MBA with Distinction, a Masters in Professional Education, and completed the AICD Company Directors Course with Order of Merit, along with CELTA and DELTA qualifications.)/Dest[13 0 R/Fit]/Parent 766 0 R/Prev 776 0 R/Next 777 0 R>>
endobj

786 0 obj
<</Title(Bec Hungerford has over 15 years\220 experience teaching English both in Australia and overseas, much of it focused on Cambridge exam preparation. She is passionate about fostering learner autonomy and encouraging curiosity about language and the wider world. She strongly believes that effective teaching should be engaging and human \204 and that motivating students and colleagues with chocolate and home-baked goods is a perfectly valid pedagogical strategy.)/Dest[14 0 R/Fit]/Parent 768 0 R/Prev 778 0 R/Next 779 0 R>>
endobj

